  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal (RNA + image) combination provides a meaningful accuracy advantage, and which core architectural choices are most impactful. Config_009 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion) tests the central multimodal hypothesis using well-established, robust components: PCA-2000 as a simple but effective RNA representation, ViT-L as the strongest available image encoder, transformer aggregation to capture cross-profile interactions, and weighted fusion to let the model learn modality importance. This provides a strong reference baseline: if it performs well, subsequent experiments can refine by swapping in more sophisticated RNA encoders (scgpt, scvi_n200) or different fusion strategies; if it underperforms, the result helps diagnose whether the bottleneck lies in the RNA encoding, image encoding, or fusion mechanism. As the first of 10 experiments, establishing this multimodal baseline is the highest-information-gain choice before committing budget to single-modality comparisons or fine-grained ablations."
}

